iv>", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "text": "", "id": 1, "correct": 0}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n3le01ob04re5aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "question"}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 1, "type": "text"}, {"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Question in Simple Present</div>", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Question in Present Continuous</div>", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n3le01ob04re5aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "question"}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 2, "type": "text"}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Are these questions in simple present or in present continuous? ", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Activity 3", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\"> Listen to clues on the left. <span class=\"bullet\"> Click on the correct box in the table. <span class=\"bullet\">There is only one answer per audio.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You have 2 attempts to submit your answers.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12, "type": "TAB"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Timmy</span>: Hi, Ashley! What are you doing? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: I'm studying for my test, but it's too much information. You study engineering, right? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Timmy</span>: Yes, I do. Why are you asking me that? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: I need your help. Do you know what an acquisition system is? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Timmy</span>: Of course I do. A data acquisition system is what gathers real-time data and converts it into electrical signals thanks to a transducer, which has certain devices to produce an output that goes to a signal conditioning circuit. Then, a data acquisition device turns the signal intro a stream of digital data.", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "42000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: That doesn't sound that difficult. What are the components of a data acquisition system? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Timmy</span>: Well, a data acquisition system may have many components. The first one, as I mentioned before, is a transducer which is a device that measures data and turns it into an equivalent electrical signal. The second component is a signal conditioning circuit which ensures that the signal fits into the range of the data acquisition device; it also isolates the signal from other waves coming from the computer, making the signal as clear as possible.  Other important components are measurement hardware and control software. They are key elements for data acquisition.", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "91000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: You are very smart, Timmy. Help me with one last thing, what is the most important component of data acquisition systems? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Timmy</span>: I would say it is the sampling rate. This component is the number of times per second the device measures a signal. The more times it measures a signal, the clearer the representation. For example, sound, if the device measures a signal many times, the sound is better. We sometimes need much resolution to display data clearly. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: Thanks a lot, Timmy. I'm sure that after your explanation, I'll get a good grade.", "image": "enpe7n3le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le01ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}